 The sweep turns flagged tasks and the git log into ADR candidates. A task closed with `adr: candidate` (see `.agents/skills/task-lifecycle/adr-check.md`) stays flagged until an ADR covers it (`recorded`) or Alexander declines it (`declined`), so the watermark only bounds the `git log` scan for decisions that never went through a task.
 
